ODE 0.5.0 (@ode) changed as the shipped bin\ode.dll is
(docs/behavior/physics-library.md sections 3-6): library-wide world
parameters, worlds as lists with bodies and joints made without one, no
auto-disabling, the whole world stepped as one group, the steppers' non-finite
guards, the row shuffle and clamping, the capped contact, the fixed joint's
pose, joint defaults, emptying a group, the normalisation, the box-box
edge-edge contacts, dGeomRaySet, the exported internals; and the arithmetic
of docs/behavior/physics-harness.md sections 2-5 (the load-time auto-disable
threshold, dNormalize3_slow, QuickStep's linear update, the quaternion
derivative, ray-sphere). Applied by Bazel to the release (MODULE.bazel);
ODE's code is used under its BSD licence option.

